{"term":"aboriginal","senses":[{"id":"kaikki:a3bb914102fa66edce","definition":"First according to historical or scientific records; original; indigenous; primitive.","example":"Green in the Church-yard, beautiful and green; / […] / And mantled o'er with aboriginal turf / And everlasting flowers.","pos":"adj","synonyms":["ancient","autochthonous","earliest","endemic","first","indigenous","native","original","primeval","primitive","primordial"],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"","wordFamily":["aboriginality","aboriginally","aboriginalness","nonaboriginal"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/aboriginal#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:06716cf5a4ce544655","definition":"Living in a land before colonization by foreigners.","example":"Where else but from Nantucket did those aboriginal whalemen, the Red-Men, first sally out in canoes to give chase to the Leviathan?","pos":"adj","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"","wordFamily":["aboriginality","aboriginally","aboriginalness","nonaboriginal"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/aboriginal#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:4a8b943668eb53ec69","definition":"Alternative letter-case form of Aboriginal","example":"","pos":"adj","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"alt-of","register":"alt-of","wordFamily":["aboriginality","aboriginally","aboriginalness","nonaboriginal"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/aboriginal#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:bce7d5c7103ff059f8","definition":"An animal or plant native to a region.","example":"It may be welldoubted whether this frog is an aboriginal of these islands.","pos":"